   "text": "I read the macrocycle region by region and wrote the SMILES around the ring.\n\n**Substituents and fragments**\n- **Aryl ring (top left):** it carries three OMe groups at the 2, 3 and 5 positions relative to the chain attachment, and the chain is CH2CH2 leading to the benzylic carbon.\n- **Benzylic carbon:** it is bonded to the ester O and to the meta-substituted phenyl ring, and the hashed bond to the CH2 sets its stereochemistry.\n- **Ester and pipecolic acid:** the ester O\u2013C(=O) is attached to an (S)-pipecolic acid, drawn with a wedge to ring C3.\n- **Keto amide and ester:** the pipecolic N carries C(=O)C(=O)C(CH3)2CH2\u2013O\u2013C(=O).\n- **Alkene:** the C=C is drawn with a wavy bond, so I gave it no cis/trans label.\n- **Sarcosine and glycine:** after the alkene come CH2\u2013N(CH3)\u2013C(=O)\u2013CH2\u2013NH\u2013C(=O).\n- **Serine:** it is O-tert-butyl, wedged to its CH2.\n- **N-Me-2-naphthylalanine:** the naphthyl is attached at the 2-position, with a wedge to the CH2.\n- **N-Me-norleucine:** it carries a wedged n-butyl group and is linked through N(CH3)\u2013C(=O)\u2013CH2\u2013O to the meta position of the phenyl ring.\n\n**Stereocentres:** I assigned the @/@@ marks from the wedges and hashes by working out the neighbour order at each centre.\n\nSMILES: COc1cc(OC)c(OC)c(c1)CC[C@H]%10OC(=O)[C@@H]2CCCCN2C(=O)C(=O)C(C)(C)COC(=O)C=CCN(C)C(=O)CNC(=O)[C@@H](COC(C)(C)C)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](Cc3ccc4ccccc4c3)NC(=O)[C@H](CCCC)N(C)C(=O)COc8cccc%10c8"
